{
  "id": "9cfkmtq",
  "title": "CHAPTER 5: ECONOMY OF ANDHRA PRADESH",
  "order": 6,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Andhra Pradesh has one of the fast-growing economies among Indian states. The state's economy is primarily agrarian but has been diversifying significantly into industry, services, and information technology.",
      "id": "9tvpc5d"
    },
    {
      "id": "x0bok45",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "id": "k0sk12r",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "7fe5cns",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Andhra_Pradesh CONSTABLE/images/image_7fe5cns.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Agriculture is the backbone of Andhra Pradesh's economy, employing a large proportion of the workforce. The state is called the 'Rice Bowl of India' owing to the fertile Krishna-Godavari delta producing enormous quantities of rice. Andhra Pradesh is one of the top producers of rice, tobacco, cotton, sugarcane, groundnut, chilli peppers, and aquaculture in India.",
      "id": "scxaume"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2vb9xd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.1 Major Crops"
    },
    {
      "id": "uzbhjki",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Crop</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rice (Paddy)</p>",
            "<p>Principal food crop; grown in Krishna-Godavari delta (kharif and rabi seasons); major varieties – Sona Masuri, BPT 5204</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tobacco</p>",
            "<p>AP is India's largest tobacco producer; grown in Guntur, Krishna, West Godavari; famous 'Virginia Tobacco'</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Chilli (Red Pepper)</p>",
            "<p>AP is India's largest chilli-producing state; Guntur famous for 'Guntur Sannam' variety; major export commodity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Groundnut</p>",
            "<p>2nd or 3rd largest producer in India; major crop in Anantapur, Kurnool, Kadapa</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cotton</p>",
            "<p>Grown in Guntur, Krishna, West Godavari, Kurnool</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sugarcane</p>",
            "<p>Grown in coastal districts and Godavari basin</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Turmeric</p>",
            "<p>Nizamabad (earlier in AP, now Telangana), but Warangal area; coastal AP also produces</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Maize</p>",
            "<p>Grown in Nellore, Guntur, Kurnool</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cashew Nuts</p>",
            "<p>Srikakulam, Vizianagaram, Visakhapatnam (East Coast)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mango</p>",
            "<p>State Fruit; Banganapalle/Banganapalli variety from Kurnool is GI-tagged</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Aquaculture (Shrimp/Prawn)</p>",
            "<p>AP is India's largest aquaculture state; Nellore, West Godavari, Krishna; major export earner</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b0ld9nr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.2 Industry"
    },
    {
      "id": "y4kxq7o",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "8qw05ja",
      "src": "/books/Guide/Andhra_Pradesh CONSTABLE/images/image_8qw05ja.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "id": "uv4quqj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.2.1 Major Industries"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Andhra Pradesh has a diverse industrial base including pharmaceuticals, cement, power generation, textiles, food processing, petroleum, and information technology.",
      "id": "5h8iind"
    },
    {
      "id": "wtiio3o",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Industry</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Areas/Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Pharmaceuticals</p>",
            "<p>Visakhapatnam, Kakinada; several bulk drug manufacturing clusters; 'Pharma City' near Visakhapatnam</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cement</p>",
            "<p>Kurnool, Kadapa, Guntur; major companies – Ultratech, Ramco, India Cements, Dalmia</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Petroleum/Refining</p>",
            "<p>HPCL Visakhapatnam Refinery (one of India's major refineries); ONGC operations offshore and onshore</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Textiles</p>",
            "<p>Chirala and Ongole for synthetic fabrics; handloom clusters in Mangalagiri, Venkatagiri, Uppada, Dharmavaram</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ship Building</p>",
            "<p>Hindustan Shipyard Limited (HSL), Visakhapatnam – one of India's first shipyards</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Steel</p>",
            "<p>RINL – Rashtriya Ispat Nigam Limited (Visakhapatnam Steel Plant / Vizag Steel) – only coastal integrated steel plant in India</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Information Technology</p>",
            "<p>Visakhapatnam (IT SEZ); Amaravati (Smart Capital city IT corridor planned)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sugar Mills</p>",
            "<p>Krishna, West Godavari, Visakhapatnam</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Food Processing</p>",
            "<p>Aquaculture processing units in coastal districts; mango and chilli processing in Guntur</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Leather</p>",
            "<p>Nellore, Visakhapatnam</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mining (Minerals)</p>",
            "<p>Limestone in Kurnool, Kadapa; Barytes in Kadapa (world-class deposits); Asbestos in Cuddapah; Manganese in Srikakulam; Uranium in Nellore</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
