        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Visakhapatnam Port</p>",
            "<p>Deepest natural port in India; one of India's largest ports by cargo handled; handles iron ore, petroleum, fertilizers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Krishnapatnam Port</p>",
            "<p>Nellore district; one of India's largest private ports; major container handling</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kakinada Port</p>",
            "<p>East Godavari; handles fish, fertilizers, petroleum products</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gangavaram Port</p>",
            "<p>Near Visakhapatnam; private port; handles coal, limestone, bauxite</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Machilipatnam Port (under development)</p>",
            "<p>Krishna district; being developed as part of Andhra Pradesh maritime policy</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5c05vxv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Power Sector"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Andhra Pradesh has a mix of thermal, hydro, solar, and wind power projects. The state has been proactive in renewable energy development.",
      "id": "gzd2yay"
    },
